      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting OCR Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting a concrete OCR provider for the `extract_text.py` script. The prompt's emphasis on a cloud-based solution and the need for code clarity strongly point towards a popular, readily-identifiable cloud OCR service. My thought process is now on identifying the optimal choice from these options.\n\n\n**Defining the `extract_text.py`**\n\nI'm now structuring the `extract_text.py` file with the intent of using Google Cloud Vision. I'm focusing on defining a function, `extract_text_from_image`, that takes the image file path as input and calls the Google Cloud Vision API to perform the OCR. I am leaning toward using the `google.cloud.vision_v1` library and I will handle client initialization within the function to clearly identify the provider. The goal is a clean, readily usable function that returns the extracted text.\n\n\n**Implementing the Script**\n\nI'm now writing the `extract_text.py` script. My focus is on implementing the `extract_text_from_image` function that uses Google Cloud Vision AI.  I've sketched out the function with necessary imports and initialization of the `vision.ImageAnnotatorClient`.  The basic structure is in place to take an image path, read the file, and then call `document_text_detection` on the content. The function should return the extracted text from the response's `full_text_annotation.text`. I'm including an example usage stub, but will remove this before delivery.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861514596,
          "start": 1789861512010
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
